    "raw": "Let's denote Ben's gross monthly income as \\( G \\). Given that he pays \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\) of his gross income in taxes, his after-tax income is \\( \\frac{2}{3}G \\).\n\nBen spends 20% of his after-tax income on his car, and this amount is $400. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\\[ 0.2 \\times \\frac{2}{3}G = 400 \\]\n\nTo find \\( G \\), we first simplify the left side of the equation:\n\\[ \\frac{0.4}{3}G = 400 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{2}{15}G = 400 \\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\( G \\) by multiplying both sides by \\( \\frac{15}{2} \\):\n\\[ G = 400 \\times \\frac{15}{2} \\]\n\\[ G = 400 \\times 7.5 \\]\n\\[ G = 3000 \\]\n\nThus, Ben's gross monthly income is $3000.\n\nFINAL: 3000",
